The tilted work plane on the two parallel machines, the hexapod sim on
genhexkins and the pentapod sim on pentakins, with their configs'
geometry.  Neither has a rotary joint: the struts set the pose, and the
tool is oriented with the pose's own angles, A B C on the hexapod and
A B on the pentapod.

From a tilted start, G68.2 defines a plane and G53.6 turns the tool to
its normal about the tool tip: the reported tool axis is the normal and
X Y Z have not moved.  On the hexapod the axis leaves the turn about it
free, and the platform takes the shortest rotation from where it stood,
no turn about the tool.  G53.1 is refused, since it turns rotary joints
alone.  G53.3 ends at the point asked for in the plane with the tool on
the normal, and G68.3 reads the plane's normal back off the tool.

The [AXIS_L] box is the platform's, its pose with the tool left out, as
the carriage is on a head: with a long tool and the platform tilted about
Y, a move whose tool pose is inside the box with the platform past it is
refused, and one whose tool pose is past it with the platform inside is
accepted.
